(Section 7. Training and development) Tj T*
(Every employee has an annual training budget of 1,200 euros for courses, conferences and) Tj T*
(certifications related to their role. Unused training budget does not carry over to the) Tj T*
(following year.) Tj T*
(Employees who receive company-funded training costing more than 3,000 euros in total must) Tj T*
(repay a share of the cost if they resign within 12 months of completing it.) Tj T*
(Section 8. Health and safety) Tj T*
(Accidents and near misses must be reported to the site safety officer on the same day.) Tj T*
(First aid kits are located next to every fire exit, and trained first aiders are listed on) Tj T*
(the notice board in each building.) Tj T*
(Fire alarm tests take place every Wednesday at 11:00. A full evacuation drill is held) Tj T*
(twice a year without prior notice.) Tj T*
(Section 9. Leaving the company) Tj T*
(The notice period is 1 month during probation and 3 months after probation. Notice must be) Tj T*
(given in writing to the line manager and copied to HR.) Tj T*
(Company equipment, including laptops, phones and access badges, must be returned on or) Tj T*
(before the last working day. Remaining annual leave is paid out with the final salary.) Tj T*
(Section 10. Contacts) Tj T*
(Questions about this handbook should be sent to the HR service desk. The handbook is) Tj T*
(reviewed every year in January by the people operations team.) Tj T*
ET
